#
# Declarative structural assertions for the inference slice (Tier-B
# closeout). The inference slice has no migratable rdflib pytest; these cells are
# authored fresh to pin its keystone invariants (MAXIMAL coverage, dogfooding).
# Each runs as a SPARQL ASK over the module graph (gmeow:scopeModule). Inference
# is the epistemic face of a logic: derivation — Peirce's tetrad (deduction,
# induction, abduction, analogy) riding one InferenceMode value vocabulary, with
# a clean gUFO endurant/occurrent split.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/inference/tests/> .

# --- 1. The reified argument relators (MUST hold) ----------------------------
ex:saInferenceRelatorKinds a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:Analogy             a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:Correspondence      a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:InferenceCommitment a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:Analogy, gmeow:Correspondence, and gmeow:InferenceCommitment MUST each be a logic:Kind owl:Class subClassOf logic:Relator — the reified, endurant argument/mapping relations (the gmeow:Commitment idiom)." .

# --- 1b. The argumentation-layer relators + named unions (MUST hold) ----------
ex:saArgumentationRelators a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:Argument           a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:ArgumentEvaluation a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:Attack             a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:Support            a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:PremiseUse         a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:InferenceApplication a owl:Class , logic:Kind ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:Relator .
    gmeow:AttackTarget       a owl:Class , logic:Category ; rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing .
    gmeow:SupportSource      a owl:Class , logic:Category ; rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The Dung/ASPIC+ argumentation layer MUST mint gmeow:Argument, gmeow:ArgumentEvaluation, gmeow:Attack, gmeow:Support, gmeow:PremiseUse, and gmeow:InferenceApplication as logic:Kind reified relators (subClassOf logic:Relator), and gmeow:AttackTarget / gmeow:SupportSource as logic:Category named-union superclasses — the attackable framework node, its solver-set verdict, the typed conflict, the accruing support, the basing premise-use, the rule-application, and the attack-target / support-source unions." .

# --- 2. Endurant/occurrent split: Process and Tenure spine (MUST hold) --------
ex:saInferenceProcessTenureSpine a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:InferenceProcess a owl:Class , logic:Event ; rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:MentalProcess .
    gmeow:InferenceTenure  a owl:Class , logic:Situation ; rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:TimeScopedRelation .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The gUFO master split MUST hold: gmeow:InferenceProcess is the OCCURRENT reasoning episode (logic:Event subClassOf gmeow:MentalProcess) and gmeow:InferenceTenure is the time-scoped situation (logic:Situation subClassOf gmeow:TimeScopedRelation) — distinct from the endurant gmeow:InferenceCommitment relator." .

# --- 3. Mode/Attack/Acceptance value vocabularies and their seeds (MUST hold) --
ex:saInferenceValueVocabs a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>
ASK {
    gmeow:InferenceMode a owl:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
    gmeow:AttackKind a owl:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
    gmeow:AcceptanceStatus a owl:Class , logic:AbstractIndividualType ; rdfs:subClassOf logic:QualityValue .
    gmeow:modeDeduction a gmeow:InferenceMode . gmeow:modeInduction a gmeow:InferenceMode .
    gmeow:modeAbduction a gmeow:InferenceMode . gmeow:modeAnalogical a gmeow:InferenceMode .
    gmeow:attackUndermine a gmeow:AttackKind . gmeow:attackUndercut a gmeow:AttackKind . gmeow:attackRebut a gmeow:AttackKind .
    gmeow:acceptanceIn a gmeow:AcceptanceStatus . gmeow:acceptanceOut a gmeow:AcceptanceStatus . gmeow:acceptanceUndecided a gmeow:AcceptanceStatus .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:InferenceMode, gmeow:AttackKind, and gmeow:AcceptanceStatus MUST be QualityValue vocabularies; the Peircean tetrad seeds (modeDeduction/modeInduction/modeAbduction/modeAnalogical), the three typed-attack kinds (undermine/undercut/rebut — subsuming the older Pollock two-way rebutting/undercutting distinction), and the Dung labelling seeds (in/out/undecided) MUST be present. These are open value vocabularies (no closure asserted)." .

# --- 4. Argument edge properties (MUST hold) ---------------------------------
ex:saInferenceFunctionalProperties a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:conclusion a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain gmeow:InferenceCommitment ; rdfs:range gmeow:StandpointClaim .
    gmeow:inferenceModeOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain gmeow:InferenceCommitment ; rdfs:range gmeow:InferenceMode .
    gmeow:correspondingSource a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:Correspondence .
    gmeow:correspondingTarget a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:domain gmeow:Correspondence .
    gmeow:tenureOf a owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain gmeow:InferenceTenure ; rdfs:range gmeow:InferenceCommitment .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "The single-valued argument edges MUST be owl:ObjectProperty with their declared domain/range: gmeow:conclusion (InferenceCommitment → StandpointClaim), gmeow:inferenceModeOf (InferenceCommitment → InferenceMode), gmeow:correspondingSource/Target (domain gmeow:Correspondence), gmeow:tenureOf (InferenceTenure → InferenceCommitment)." .

# --- 5. competesWith is a symmetric StandpointClaim relation (MUST hold) ------
ex:saCompetesWithSymmetric a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:must ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    gmeow:competesWith a owl:SymmetricProperty , owl:ObjectProperty ;
        rdfs:domain gmeow:StandpointClaim ; rdfs:range gmeow:StandpointClaim .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "gmeow:competesWith MUST be an owl:SymmetricProperty (competition is mutual) over gmeow:StandpointClaim — the rivalry abductive/analogical selection resolves. Irreflexivity stays in SHACL, not OWL, keeping the DL profile clean." .

# --- 6. Modes ride one class, never a taxonomy (MUST-NOT hold) ----------------
ex:saInferenceCommitmentNoSubclasses a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK { ?c rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:InferenceCommitment . FILTER (?c != gmeow:InferenceCommitment) }""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Principle 9 (no overtyping): the four Peircean modes differ by a VALUE + a WARRANT, never by subsumption, so the module MUST NOT declare any subclass of gmeow:InferenceCommitment. A deductive vs abductive step is an gmeow:inferenceModeOf value, not a class." .

# --- 6b. The argumentation node rides one class, never a taxonomy (MUST-NOT) ---
ex:saArgumentNoSubclasses a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK { ?c rdfs:subClassOf gmeow:Argument . FILTER (?c != gmeow:Argument) }""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Principle 9 (no overtyping): a gmeow:Argument's variety is a matter of the typed gmeow:Attack / gmeow:Support relations it bears and its gmeow:ArgumentEvaluation, never subsumption, so the module MUST NOT declare any subclass of gmeow:Argument." .

# --- 7. Open-range argument properties: NO rdfs:range (MUST-NOT hold) ---------
ex:saInferenceOpenRanges a gmeow:StructuralAssertion ;
    gmeow:saPolarity gmeow:mustNot ;
    gmeow:saScope gmeow:scopeModule ;
    gmeow:saPattern """PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
ASK {
    VALUES ?p {
        gmeow:premise gmeow:inferredFrom gmeow:warrant gmeow:explains gmeow:explanandum
        gmeow:analogicalSource gmeow:analogicalTarget gmeow:correspondingSource gmeow:correspondingTarget
        gmeow:argumentConclusion gmeow:premiseUsed gmeow:appliedRule gmeow:attackSource
    }
    ?p rdfs:range ?r .
}""" ;
    gmeow:saRationale "Principle 13: the argument/mapping inputs are open-range — a premise, warrant, explanandum, mapped element, argument conclusion, used premise, applied rule, or attack source may be any entity, claim, or proposition. None of these properties MUST declare an rdfs:range. VALUES ranges over the fixed, closed set of open-range properties the inference slice declares (not a stand-in for an open universal)." .
